  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user with several accounts, I want the account menu to mark the current account with the system selection checkmark, with every row aligned, so that the menu reads as a standard choice list.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Apply a uniform visual treatment across menu items in the same group. For visual consistency and balance, provide icons for all menu items in a group, or none of them.\" and \"Consider using a checkmark to show that an attribute is currently in effect.\" — [HIG › Menus](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/menus) (Icons, Toggled items; page updated 2026-06-08).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Accounts/AccountMenuButton.swift:34-38`: `if row.isMain { Label(row.displayName, systemImage: \"checkmark\") } else { Text(row.displayName) }`: the selected state is drawn as the item's icon, so one row of the group has an icon and the others have none.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\n`HFRswift/Swift/AccountMenuViews.swift:15-25`: every row is a `Label` with the avatar as icon and the checkmark after the name: uniform. SwiftHFR is worse.\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect** (parity), low.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Make the account rows an inline `Picker` bound to the current account id: the system draws its checkmark and the VoiceOver selected state (the `.isSelected` trait at `:42` becomes redundant). Avatars as icons can come with #425.\n- Mac check: the menu with two or more accounts shows aligned names and one system checkmark.\n\nRelated: #425, #430 (same menu, other topics).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
